Be very rigorous about reading the current codebase in @/src Especially before adding new modules, files or functions to make sure you are not missing anything that could be used/modified instead. A good structure is paramount.

### Most important packages:
[__init__.py](mdc:src/common_types/__init__.py) (@/src/common_types) This module contains type definitions that are reused across the code base.
It provides standardized type hints to ensure consistency and improve code quality.

[__init__.py](mdc:src/agent/__init__.py) (@/src/agent) This module implements the agent system that powers the application.
It contains classes and functions for creating, managing, and executing agents
that can perform various tasks and interact with each other.

[__init__.py](mdc:src/cli/__init__.py) (@/src/cli) This module provides the command-line interface for the application.
It contains functions and classes for parsing command-line arguments,
displaying output, and managing user interactions through the terminal.

[__init__.py](mdc:src/config/__init__.py) (@/src/config) This module handles application configuration management.
It provides functionality for loading, validating, and accessing
configuration settings from various sources like files or environment variables.

[__init__.py](mdc:src/llm_providers/__init__.py) (@/src/llm_providers) This module contains integrations with various Large Language Model providers.
It abstracts the differences between different LLM APIs and provides
a unified interface for interacting with language models.

[__init__.py](mdc:src/messages/__init__.py) (@/src/messages) This module implements the message system used for communication between components.
It defines message types, formats, and handling mechanisms to facilitate
structured information exchange throughout the application.

[__init__.py](mdc:src/prompts/__init__.py) (@/src/prompts) This module manages prompt templates and generation for LLM interactions.
It provides utilities for creating, formatting, and optimizing prompts
to effectively communicate with language models.

[__init__.py](mdc:src/utils/__init__.py) (@/src/utils) This module contains general utility functions and helper classes.
It provides common functionality that is used across different parts
of the application to avoid code duplication.

You can also refer to the tests to understand the current intention of the program better. The tests are in @/tests, mostly divided between @/tests/unit & @/tests/integration